Pinned build-tools bundles for **FreeBSD {{ release }}** — tarballs of FreeBSD `.pkg` files (with full dependency trees) so [daemonless/dbuild](https://github.com/daemonless/dbuild) can install CI tooling without reaching `pkg.FreeBSD.org` at build time.

## Assets

### `freebsd-{{ release }}-*.tar.gz` — base bundle

Core build tooling:

- **podman** {{ podman_version }} + `sysutils/podman-compose`
- **buildah** {{ buildah_version }} / **skopeo** / **jq**
- **trivy** {{ trivy_version }} (image scanning)
- **python3** + `devel/py-pyyaml`
- **appjail** + **ocijail** (jail runtimes)

### `freebsd-{{ release }}-screenshot-*.tar.gz` — screenshot add-on

Extra packages for CIT `mode: screenshot`:

- **chromium** {{ chromium_version }}
- **py311-selenium** {{ selenium_version }}
- **py311-scikit-image** {{ scikit_version }}

> **Requires the base bundle.** The screenshot bundle is *incremental* — it ships only the packages **not** already in the base bundle, so install the base bundle first, then layer this on top.
